# Documentation

`docs/architecture.md` is the living source of truth alongside the code. Update it in the **same cycle** as the change that alters behavior — never as a follow-up chore.

Code and docs disagreeing is a bug, not a stale doc. Do not commit a behavior change without the matching docs edit.

## What to keep current

When a change touches any of these, update the corresponding section:

- Purpose and data model (entities, fields, enums)
- Layering and import rules
- Derived computations (streak, adherence, goal progress, pace) — precise definitions, not summaries
- Implemented API endpoints and CLI commands, including status (planned / implemented)
- Configuration (`ATLAS_DB`, `ATLAS_TZ`, bind address)
- Development log: append one entry per cycle (date, todo id, what landed)

Do not duplicate `docs/architecture.md` into the README. Link to it instead.

```markdown
# ❌ BAD — commit the feature, "docs later"
# (docs/architecture.md still lists POST /entries as planned)

# ✅ GOOD — same commit updates status and the development log
# Implemented endpoints: POST /entries
# Development log: 2026-08-12 — services — log_entry + amend_entry
```
